# THE SIFREI ROWS OF PISKAOT 189-190 (THE DEUTERONOMY WALK sitting 16 — CHAPTERS 19-21, LEAN, 2026-09-24): violence is robbery, "sarah" a transgression with
# 13:6 and Jeremiah 28:16, the witness liable when he contradicts himself — Makkot 1:4's refuted witnesses (189); the judges sit and the litigants stand, two men
# and any two, the woman's testimony by the two "two"s, the ox's owner, before the Omnipresent, the judge of your days, "well" and "well" the seven questions,
# the probes from 13:15, the witness who falsifies himself and his fellow, until the verdict, a hundred refuted, as he plotted in money, lashes and death, the
# warning Exodus 20:13, the Sadducees' "life for life", the priest's daughter's strangling, the shame paid in money, hand and foot money, R. Yose the Galilean's
# whole soldier, the obligatory war's bridegroom, one horse — the piska running past into 20:1: optional war, your enemies, horse for horse, the One who brought
# you up (190). Every row READ WHOLE; the prior reads REREAD WHOLE and marked; the cuts by ch19_ink.SP_. Sitting 15's form.
from ch19_ink import *
S = {}
def srow(p, r, verdict, prose): S[(p, r)] = (verdict, prose)

srow(189, 1, 'MATERIAL', f'"WHEN A VIOLENT WITNESS RISES AGAINST A MAN TO TESTIFY SARAH (A TURNING) AGAINST HIM" (19:16) — VIOLENCE IS NOTHING BUT A ROBBER; SARAH IS NOTHING BUT A TRANSGRESSION, AS IT SAYS "FOR HE SPOKE SARAH" (13:6) AND "THIS YEAR YOU DIE, FOR YOU SPOKE SARAH AGAINST THE LORD" (JEREMIAH 28:16). ({SP_(189, 1, "אין", "חמס", "אלא", "גזלן")} "violence is nothing but a robber"; {SP_(189, 1, "אין", "סרה", "אלא", "עברה")} "sarah is nothing but a transgression"): THE FALSE WITNESS\'S TWO WORDS DEFINED — the "violent" one a robber (Exodus 23:1\'s ed chamas), the charge a transgression (the seducer\'s and Hananiah\'s word) — the compile\'s witness case keyed on a charged transgression. REREAD WHOLE (chapter 13, deu_13_reeh).')
srow(189, 2, 'MATERIAL', f'"TO TESTIFY AGAINST HIM" — HE IS NOT LIABLE UNTIL HE CONTRADICTS HIMSELF; FROM HERE THEY SAID (MAKKOT 1:4): WITNESSES ARE NOT MADE ZOMEMIM (REFUTED) UNTIL THEY THEMSELVES ARE REFUTED — HOW? "I TESTIFY OF SO-AND-SO THAT HE KILLED" … ({SP_(189, 2, "עד", "שיכחיש", "את", "עצמו")} "until he contradicts himself"; {SP_(189, 2, "אין", "העדים", "נעשים", "זוממים")} "the witnesses are not made refuted"): THE SECOND EXAM ROW — Makkot 1:4 cited by chapter and mishnah in the Hebrew: refutation is of the WITNESSES\' PERSONS ("you were with us that day"), not of their story — the compile\'s zomemim cell keyed on the alibi of the witnesses, not the deed; the English supplies the Mishnah\'s remainder in braces. Fresh.')
srow(190, 1, 'MATERIAL', f'"AND THEY SHALL STAND" (19:17) — THE JUDGES SIT AND THE LITIGANTS STAND. ANOTHER WORD: A WARNING TO THE LITIGANT NOT TO PLEAD BEFORE HIS OPPONENT COMES. "AND THEY SHALL STAND" — A COMMANDMENT ON THE JUDGED TO STAND. ({SP_(190, 1, "הדינים", "יושבים", "ובעלי", "דינים", "עומדים")} "the judges sit and the litigants stand"; {SP_(190, 1, "קודם", "שיבא", "בעל", "דין", "חברו")} "before his opposing litigant comes"): THE COURT\'S POSTURE (Shevuot 30a\'s rule, not opened; the English marks the row as interpolated in most versions) and the bar on ex-parte pleading (the Mekhilta on Exodus 23:1) — the compile\'s procedure parameters. Fresh.')
srow(190, 2, 'MATERIAL', f'"THE TWO MEN" — I HAVE ONLY TWO MEN; A MAN WITH A WOMAN, A WOMAN WITH A MAN, TWO WOMEN? "WHO HAVE THE DISPUTE" — IN ANY CASE. ({SP_(190, 2, "שתי", "נשים", "זו", "עם", "זו")} "two women with each other"; {SP_(190, 2, "מכל", "מקום")} "in any case"): THE LITIGANTS ANY — "men" not restrictive for the parties (Shevuot 30a); the compile\'s parties parameter. Fresh.')
srow(190, 3, 'MATERIAL', f'MIGHT A WOMAN BE FIT TO TESTIFY? "TWO" IS SAID HERE AND "TWO" IS SAID THERE (19:15): AS THE "TWO" THERE ARE MEN AND NOT WOMEN, SO HERE. ({SP_(190, 3, "אף", "אשה", "תהא", "כשרה", "לעדות")} "even a woman be fit to testify"; {SP_(190, 3, "אנשים", "ולא", "נשים")} "men and not women"): THE WITNESSES MEN by the analogy of the two "two"s (the gezerah shavah on 19:15 and 19:17 — 17:6 the English\'s alternate seat) — the compile\'s witness-class parameter (the Sifrei read this row at 17:6 too). REREAD WHOLE (chapters 17-18, deu_17_18_shoftim).')
srow(190, 4, 'MATERIAL', f'"WHO HAVE THE DISPUTE" — LET THE OWNER OF THE OX COME AND STAND BY HIS OX. ({SP_(190, 4, "יבוא", "בעל", "השור", "ויעמד", "על", "שורו")} "let the owner of the ox come and stand by his ox"): THE GORING OX\'S TRIAL needs its owner present (Exodus 21:29 — Sanhedrin 1:4\'s "the ox is judged like its owner", Bava Kamma 45a, not opened) — the compile\'s cross-call to the ordinances\' ox (the presence parameter). Fresh.')
srow(190, 5, 'CONTEXT', f'"BEFORE THE LORD" — THEY THINK THEY STAND BEFORE FLESH AND BLOOD, BUT THEY STAND BEFORE THE OMNIPRESENT. ({SP_(190, 5, "לפני", "בשר", "ודם")} "before flesh and blood"; {SP_(190, 5, "לפני", "המקום")} "before the Omnipresent"): the court\'s presence the Presence — 1:17\'s "the judgment is God\'s" in another form; no rule. Fresh.')
srow(190, 6, 'MATERIAL', f'"BEFORE THE PRIESTS AND THE JUDGES WHO WILL BE IN THOSE DAYS" — R. YOSE THE GALILEAN: WOULD IT OCCUR TO US A JUDGE NOT IN YOUR DAYS? A JUDGE FIT AND ESTABLISHED FOR YOU IN THOSE DAYS; WAS A KINSMAN AND BECAME REMOTE — FIT; "SAY NOT, WHY WERE THE FORMER DAYS BETTER" (ECCLESIASTES 7:10). ({SP_(190, 6, "שופט", "שאינו", "בימיך")} "a judge who is not in your days"; {SP_(190, 6, "היה", "קרוב", "ונתרחק", "כשר")} "was a kinsman and became remote — fit"): "IN THOSE DAYS" = the judge of your own day (17:9\'s twin, 153:2 the same teaching) — the kinsman-turned-stranger fit (Sanhedren 28a\'s rule, not opened); the compile\'s judge-fitness parameter. Fresh.')
srow(190, 7, 'MATERIAL', f'"AND THE JUDGES SHALL INQUIRE WELL" (19:18) — AND THERE IT SAYS "AND IT IS TOLD YOU AND YOU HEAR AND INQUIRE WELL" (17:4): "WELL" AND "WELL" A GEZERAH SHAVAH, TEACHING THAT THEY EXAMINE HIM WITH SEVEN INVESTIGATIONS. I HAVE ONLY INVESTIGATIONS; PROBES? "AND BEHOLD IT IS TRUE, THE THING IS CERTAIN" (13:15). ({SP_(190, 7, "היטב", "היטב", "לגזרה", "שוה")} "well, well — an analogy of equal words"; {SP_(190, 7, "בשבע", "חקירות")} "with seven investigations"): THE SEVEN INVESTIGATIONS AT THEIR THIRD SEAT (13:15, 17:4, 19:18 — Sanhedrin 5:1 the answer sheet; the probes from "true and certain") — the compile\'s inquiry cell shared over the three laws (the seducers\', the idolater\'s, the witnesses\'). REREAD WHOLE (chapter 13 and chapters 17-18, deu_13_reeh and deu_17_18_shoftim).')
srow(190, 8, 'MATERIAL', f'WHENCE THAT THE WITNESS MAKES HIMSELF FALSE? THE TEACHING SAYS "AND BEHOLD THE WITNESS IS A FALSE WITNESS". ({SP_(190, 8, "שהעד", "עושה", "עצמו", "שקר")} "that the witness makes himself false"): the English carries 13:15\'s probes here and the Hebrew the first of two "false" readings — the witness\'s own falsification counts (Sanhedrin 5:2 the English\'s note). REREAD WHOLE (chapter 13, deu_13_reeh).')
srow(190, 9, 'MATERIAL', f'AND WHENCE THAT HE MAKES HIS FELLOW FALSE? "AND BEHOLD THE WITNESS IS A FALSE WITNESS". MIGHT IT BE EVEN AFTER THEIR TESTIMONY WAS EXAMINED IN COURT? "HE TESTIFIED FALSELY AGAINST HIS BROTHER" — SAY FROM NOW: AS LONG AS THE COURT NEEDS THEM, NOT ONCE THEIR TESTIMONY WAS EXAMINED. WHEN YOU FIND IT SAID: A REFUTED FROM A REFUTED, EVEN A HUNDRED. ({SP_(190, 9, "כל", "זמן", "שבית", "דין", "צריכים", "להם")} "as long as the court needs them"; {SP_(190, 9, "ואפלו", "הם", "מאה")} "and even if they are a hundred"): THE WINDOW OF REFUTATION and its chain (Makkot 1:5 the English\'s note — a hundred pairs refuted by one) — the compile\'s refutation timing and its recursion. Fresh.')
srow(190, 10, 'MATERIAL', f'"AND YOU SHALL DO TO HIM AS HE PLOTTED TO DO TO HIS BROTHER" (19:19) — IF MONEY, MONEY; IF LASHES, LASHES; IF PUNISHMENTS, PUNISHMENTS. ({SP_(190, 10, "אם", "ממון", "ממון")} "if money — money"; {SP_(190, 10, "אם", "מכות", "מכות")} "if lashes — lashes"): THE TALION OF THE PLOT — the refuted witness suffers the penalty he sought, in kind (Makkot 1:1-3 the answer sheet) — the compile\'s verdict a mirror of the plotted verdict (the three kinds). Fresh.')
srow(190, 11, 'MATERIAL', f'THE PUNISHMENT WE HEARD; THE WARNING? THE TEACHING SAYS "YOU SHALL NOT ANSWER AGAINST YOUR NEIGHBOR A FALSE WITNESS" (EXODUS 20:13). ({SP_(190, 11, "ענש", "שמענו", "אזהרה", "מנין")} "the punishment we heard; the warning — whence?"): THE DECALOGUE\'S NINTH WORD the prohibition behind the refuted witness\'s penalty (the Mekhilta\'s form; the citation supplied by the editor) — the compile\'s warning edge to the Exodus 20 line (the measure: "witness of falsehood" at Exodus 20:16 in the DB\'s numbering and 19:18). Fresh.')
srow(190, 12, 'MATERIAL', f'"AND YOU SHALL DO TO HIM" — FROM HERE THEY SAID: REFUTED WITNESSES ARE NOT KILLED UNTIL THE VERDICT IS FINISHED; FOR THE SADDUCEES SAY: UNTIL HE IS KILLED, AS IT SAYS "LIFE FOR LIFE" (19:21). ({SP_(190, 12, "עד", "שיגמר", "הדין")} "until the verdict is finished"; {SP_(190, 12, "שהרי", "צדוקים", "אומרים")} "for the Sadducees say"): THE TIMING AGAINST THE SADDUCEES — the plot punished once the verdict is sealed, before execution (Makkot 1:6 the answer sheet) — the compile\'s condition (verdict sealed; victim alive). Fresh.')
srow(190, 13, 'MATERIAL', f'R. YOSE THE GALILEAN: WHY "AS HE PLOTTED TO DO TO HIS BROTHER"? IN ALL THE TORAH\'S PUNISHMENTS THE MAN\'S DEATH EQUALS THE WOMAN\'S AND THEIR REFUTERS LIKEWISE; BUT THE PRIEST\'S DAUGHTER AND HER PARAMOUR — HE BY STRANGLING, SHE BY BURNING; THEIR REFUTERS? "AS HE PLOTTED TO DO TO HIS BROTHER" — AS HIS BROTHER\'S DEATH, NOT HIS SISTER\'S. ({SP_(190, 13, "מיתת", "האיש", "בחנק", "ומיתת", "האשה", "בשרפה")} "the man\'s death by strangling and the woman\'s by burning"; {SP_(190, 13, "כמיתת", "אחיו", "מיתתו")} "as his brother\'s death is his death"): "HIS BROTHER" LITERAL — the refuters of the priest\'s daughter\'s witnesses die the man\'s death, not the woman\'s burning (Leviticus 21:9; Sanhedrin 9:1, not opened) — the compile\'s mirror keyed on the male party. Fresh.')
srow(190, 14, 'MATERIAL', f'WHENCE THAT ONE WHO SHAMES PAYS MONEY? "YOUR EYE SHALL NOT PITY" IS SAID HERE (19:21) AND "YOUR EYE SHALL NOT PITY" THERE (25:12): AS THERE MONEY, SO HERE MONEY. ({SP_(190, 14, "שהמביש", "משלם", "ממון")} "that one who shames pays money"): THE TALION IS MONEY by the gezerah shavah with the hand cut off (25:12 — the Sifrei 293:2 the same row read from the other end, this ledger\'s outside row) — the compile\'s talion an assessment (Bava Kamma 8:1 the answer sheet). Fresh.')
srow(190, 15, 'MATERIAL', f'R. JUDAH: "HAND AND FOOT" IS SAID HERE AND "HAND AND FOOT" THERE (EXODUS 21:24): AS THERE MONEY, SO HERE MONEY. ({SP_(190, 15, "יד", "ורגל")} "hand and foot"): THE SECOND PROOF — Exodus 21:24\'s "tachat" read as money at the Mekhilta, Deuteronomy\'s "be-" (the measure\'s find: the preposition changed) carried by the words hand and foot; the compile\'s cross-call to the ordinances\' talion cell. Fresh.')
srow(190, 16, 'MATERIAL', f'R. YOSE THE GALILEAN: WHENCE THAT A MAN DOES NOT GO OUT TO WAR UNLESS HE HAS HANDS AND FEET AND EYES AND TEETH? THE TEACHING SAYS "YOUR EYE SHALL NOT PITY, LIFE FOR LIFE …" AND "WHEN YOU GO OUT TO WAR" (19:21-20:1). ({SP_(190, 16, "שלא", "יצא", "למלחמה")} "that he does not go out to war"; {SP_(190, 16, "ידים", "ורגלים", "ועינים", "ושנים")} "hands and feet and eyes and teeth"): 20:1 READ AS 19:21\'S CONTINUATION across the chapter — the soldier whole (the four limbs the talion\'s list) — the war law\'s first parameter taught inside chapter 19\'s piska. Fresh.')
srow(190, 17, 'MATERIAL', f'R. JUDAH: OF WHAT IS THIS SAID? OF A COMMANDED WAR (MITZVAH); BUT IN AN OBLIGATORY WAR (CHOVAH) ALL GO OUT, EVEN "THE BRIDEGROOM FROM HIS CHAMBER AND THE BRIDE FROM HER CANOPY" (JOEL 2:16). "HORSE AND CHARIOT" (20:1) — WHEN ISRAEL DOES THE WILL OF THE OMNIPRESENT ALL THE NATIONS BECOME BEFORE THEM AS ONE HORSE, "HORSE AND ITS RIDER HE THREW INTO THE SEA" (EXODUS 15:1). ({SP_(190, 17, "במלחמת", "מצוה")} "in a commanded war"; {SP_(190, 17, "במלחמת", "חובה", "הכל", "יוצאים")} "in an obligatory war all go out"; {SP_(190, 17, "כסוס", "אחד")} "as one horse"): THE TWO KINDS OF WAR — the exemptions in one, none in the other (Sotah 8:7 the answer sheet, the terms swapped between the manuscripts — the English\'s notes; 198:1 says it as "optional" against "commanded"): the compile\'s war-kind parameter with the vocabulary\'s dispute; the horse singular the Mekhilta\'s. Fresh.')
srow(190, 18, 'MATERIAL', f'"WHEN YOU GO OUT TO WAR AGAINST YOUR ENEMIES" (20:1) — THE VERSE SPEAKS OF AN OPTIONAL WAR. ({SP_(190, 18, "במלחמת", "הרשות", "הכתוב", "מדבר")} "the verse speaks of an optional war"): THE CHAPTER\'S OPENING keyed to the optional war (199:1 and 203:1 say it again for the siege) — the compile\'s war law scoped to "reshut" (the seven nations\' war another daemon, 7:1-2 and 20:16-18). Fresh.')
srow(190, 19, 'MATERIAL', f'"AGAINST YOUR ENEMIES" — AGAINST YOUR ENEMIES YOU FIGHT. ({SP_(190, 19, "כנגד", "אויביך", "אתה", "נלחם")} "against your enemies you fight"): the war\'s object your own enemies (192:2 the brothers excluded) — the compile\'s enemy parameter. Fresh.')
srow(190, 20, 'MATERIAL', f'"AND YOU SEE HORSE AND CHARIOT" — AS THEY COME OUT AGAINST YOU WITH HORSE AND CHARIOT, YOU TOO GO OUT AGAINST THEM WITH HORSE AND CHARIOT; AS THEY WITH A GREAT PEOPLE, YOU TOO WITH A GREAT PEOPLE. ({SP_(190, 20, "אף", "אתה", "צא", "עליהם", "בסוס", "ורכב")} "you too go out against them with horse and chariot"): THE MATCHED ARMS — the verse a permission to arm alike (the king\'s horses at 17:16 bounded, the army\'s not) — the compile\'s note. Fresh.')
srow(190, 21, 'MATERIAL', f'"FEAR THEM NOT, FOR THE LORD YOUR GOD IS WITH YOU WHO BROUGHT YOU UP FROM THE LAND OF EGYPT" — HE WHO BROUGHT YOU UP FROM EGYPT IS WITH YOU IN THE TIME OF TROUBLE. ({SP_(190, 21, "הוא", "עמך", "בעת", "צרה")} "He is with you in the time of trouble"): the receipt of the exodus as the ground of the war\'s courage (193:1 the same with the wilderness; Onkelos "His Memra is your help") — the compile\'s reference row to the tape\'s exodus. Fresh.')
